WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.900
KATIE COURIC (VOICEOVER):

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.066
is shifting before our eyes.

00:00:04.066 --> 00:00:06.834
Race you to the top, Mike.

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.233
(VOICEOVER) Big changes--

00:00:08.233 --> 00:00:09.066
Hi, Henry.

00:00:09.066 --> 00:00:10.400
HENRY: Hi, Katie.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.900
KATIE COURIC (VOICEOVER):
--big challenges--

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.800
I hate to admit it, but
I probably am prejudiced.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.400
KATIE COURIC (VOICEOVER):
--in a world that's

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.633
more complicated than ever.

00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:19.300
How many of you
have been chipped?

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.033
That kind of creeps me out.

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:22.367
[laughter]

00:00:23.533 --> 00:00:25.600
Would you consider
yourself a neo-Nazi?

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.667
I would non.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:28.367
I'd consider myself
a white nationalist,

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:30.333
and I would consider myself
a member of the alt right.

00:00:30.333 --> 00:00:34.100
We're teaching kids that
girls are second-class citizens.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.400
HR has become HER.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.000
You think this
was a hate crime?

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.033
Without a doubt.

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:41.934
She died because of her hijab.

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:46.467
American Muslims are
shaped by American culture.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:48.400
Tech addiction, there
are a lot of positives,

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.166
but there's some negative too.

00:00:50.166 --> 00:00:52.233
I want to be your best
friend and much more.

00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:54.433
Maybe not the much more part.

00:00:54.433 --> 00:00:57.934
But the friends part,
I'm cool with that.

00:00:57.934 --> 00:01:02.000
(VOICEOVER) It seems that
everyone has something to say.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:02.934
Whose streets?

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:04.000
Our streets.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.533
- Whose streets?
- Our street.

00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:07.066
KATIE COURIC (VOICEOVER): But
nobody's really listening.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:08.967
What about my rights?

00:01:08.967 --> 00:01:11.467
Don't I have rights?

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:12.734
KATIE COURIC
(VOICEOVER): Join me

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:15.800
on a journey as I
criss-cross the country,

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.400
meeting all kinds of
Americans, where they

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:23.767
live, work, pray, and play.

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:24.900
Who are we?

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.367
What do we stand for?

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:28.767
We're trying to get paid
what white women get paid.

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:30.433
KATIE COURIC (VOICEOVER):
Where are we going,

00:01:30.433 --> 00:01:32.100
and how do we make
things better?

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.133
This is [inaudible].

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:34.633
She's running for city council.

00:01:34.633 --> 00:01:35.834
Hey, how are you?

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.500
KATIE COURIC (VOICEOVER):
Searching for truth--

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.400
You actually think you're
part of the cleaning crew?

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.734
Yes.

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.367
KATIE COURIC (VOICEOVER):
--looking for understanding--

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:43.200
How would you describe what
it's like to be Muslim?

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.533
- Hard.
- Hard?

00:01:44.533 --> 00:01:46.233
(VOICEOVER) --getting to
the heart of the matter.

00:01:46.233 --> 00:01:48.400
To have such
conversations, you have to be

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.867
willing to be uncomfortable.

00:01:49.867 --> 00:01:53.800
KATIE COURIC (VOICEOVER):
--in "America Inside Out."

